{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{\n  \"question_material\": [\n    {\n      \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n      \"examples\": [\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Derosa et al. (2018)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"提供早期临床证据，显示抗生素暴露与免疫治疗预后不良相关，并指出不同肿瘤类型中PFS和OS的差异，为时间窗口效应提供初步背景。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在晚期肾细胞癌（RCC）和非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者中，ICI启动前30天内使用抗生素与更短的无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）相关。在RCC中，抗生素暴露还与更高的原发性疾病进展率相关；而在NSCLC中，多变量调整后仅OS显著缩短，PFS不显著。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"回顾性多中心分析；RCC患者（N=121）接受抗PD-(L)1治疗，NSCLC患者（N=239）接受抗PD-(L)1治疗；抗生素定义为ICI启动前≤60天使用。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R11\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Pinato et al. (2019)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"直接回答关于“预处理 vs 同时暴露”的问题，明确区分了两种暴露时间窗对预后的不同影响，是支持时间依赖性效应的关键研究。\",\n          \"finding\": \"仅在ICI启动前30天内使用的抗生素（pATB）与显著的预后不良（OS缩短、反应率降低）相关；而ICI期间同时使用的抗生素（cATB）与生存受损无关。这种关联在调整抗生素类别、体能状态和皮质类固醇使用后仍然显著。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"前瞻性多中心队列研究；196名接受ICI治疗的实体瘤患者（包括NSCLC和黑色素瘤）；严格区分pATB（ICI前30天）和cATB（ICI期间）。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R10\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Chorti et al. (2024)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"在高度免疫敏感的黑色素瘤中验证时间依赖性效应，进一步支持预处理暴露是关键风险因素，而同时暴露无影响。\",\n          \"finding\": \"ICI启动前60天内使用抗生素独立关联于更差的PFS和OS；而ICI开始后使用抗生素未与预后受损相关。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"大型多中心回顾性队列；578名接受一线抗PD-1治疗的初治晚期黑色素瘤患者；抗生素定义为ICI前或期间≤60天使用。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R17\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Alshammari et al. (2024)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"提供特定肿瘤类型（HCC）中同时暴露影响的证据，作为对比案例，显示在某些复杂临床背景下同时暴露也可能有害，但需谨慎解释。\",\n          \"finding\": \"在Child-Pugh A级晚期肝细胞癌患者中，与抗PD-1治疗同时使用抗生素与OS降低相关。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"多中心回顾性研究；59名接受Nivolumab治疗的Child-Pugh A级或早期B级肝硬化HCC患者；抗生素定义为与Nivolumab同时使用。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R20\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Tsikala-Vafea et al. (2021)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"通过Meta分析提供抗生素暴露与预后不良之间关联强度的定量证据，尽管存在异质性，但信号稳健。\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗生素暴露与多种肿瘤类型ICI治疗患者的较差OS和PFS显著相关。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"系统综述与Meta分析；12,794名ICI治疗患者；抗生素定义为ICI期间或之后<1个月，或ICI之前>1个月使用。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R25\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"attribution\": \"Crespin et al. (2023)\",\n          \"use_in_review\": \"提供最大规模的Meta分析证据，确认抗生素暴露（特别是围治疗期）与OS、PFS、ORR降低及PD风险增加的相关性，强化证据强度。\",\n          \"finding\": \"ICI启动前后的抗生素暴露一致关联于较差的OS和PFS、较低的客观缓解率（ORR）以及更高的疾病进展（PD）风险，且在ICI启动前后不久给药时负面效应最强。\",\n          \"conditions\": \"系统综述与Meta分析；超过41,000名ICI治疗癌症患者；抗生素定义多样，主要关注ICI启动前后。\",\n          \"reference_ids\": [\n            \"R27\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"关于抗生素类别特异性效应的共识：目前大多数回顾性研究和Meta分析并未发现抗生素类别之间存在统计学上的显著差异，这主要归因于统计效能不足、暴露定义异质性以及缺乏详细的累积剂量和持续时间报告。然而，文献指出β-内酰胺类和氟喹诺酮类是最常用的抗生素，且已知它们对肠道微生物多样性有深远且持久的影响。作者推测，抗生素的作用谱（spectrum of activity）而非抗生素类别本身可能是干扰免疫治疗的关键决定因素。窄谱抗生素或较短疗程可能在理论上具有较少的负面免疫调节作用，但这一假设在临床环境中尚未得到充分验证。\\n\\n关于预处理与同时暴露的证据强度：现有临床证据强烈支持时间依赖性效应。预处理暴露（通常在ICI启动前30-60天内） consistently 与预后不良（OS和PFS缩短、原发性耐药增加）相关，而同时暴露（concurrent exposure）的影响则更具可变性，部分研究显示无显著影响，部分在特定复杂背景下（如HCC）显示负面影响。这种时间关系的生物学合理性在于，早期的微生物群破坏可能损害免疫治疗启动时的免疫 priming（致敏），而随后的扰动可能影响较小。Meta分析提供了强有力的定量支持，证实了这一关联的稳健性，尽管由于观察性数据的局限性，因果关系仍不能最终确立。\",\n      \"remaining_points\": [\n        \"抗生素类别特异性效应的确切机制尚不明确，需要前瞻性试验系统评估抗生素类别、作用谱、持续时间和时间与ICI启动的关系。\",\n        \"感染严重程度和适应症混杂因素难以完全排除，限制了因果推断。\",\n        \"微生物组 profiling 在大多数临床研究中未常规进行，阻碍了抗生素诱导的微生物变化与免疫治疗结果之间的直接相关性分析。\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Understand User Goal:** The user wants a structured JSON output containing research notes for a literature review. The specific question to address is: \"What is the consensus on antibiotic class-specific effects? What is the strength of evidence for pre-treatment vs concurrent exposure?\"\n    - Output format: `{\"question_material\": [{\"question_id\": \"...\", \"examples\": [...], \"explanation\": \"...\", \"remaining_points\": []}]}`\n    - `examples`: Each note belongs to one paper/study. Must include `attribution`, `use_in_review`, `finding`, `conditions`, `reference_ids`.\n    - `explanation`: Concepts, principles, mechanisms, author's synthesis related to the question. No cross-study generalizations not explicitly stated. Specific, clear.\n    - `remaining_points`: Important unanswered questions from the text.\n    - Language: Chinese (retain necessary terms).\n    - Constraints: Do not merge different studies. Keep quantitative results with their metrics/subjects. Distinguish direct answers from background/comparisons. Only use info actually provided in the text.\n\n2.  **Analyze the Source Text for the Question:**\n    *Question:* Consensus on antibiotic class-specific effects? Strength of evidence for pre-treatment vs concurrent exposure?\n    *Scan for \"antibiotic class-specific effects\" / \"class\" / \"beta-lactams\" / \"fluoroquinolones\":*\n    - Section \"Role of antibiotic classes and spectrum of activity\": \"An unresolved question concerns whether the detrimental association... is driven by specific antibiotic classes or reflects a broader effect of microbiome disruption. Most retrospective studies and meta-analyses included in this review were not designed to detect class-specific effects and generally reported no statistically significant differences between antibiotic categories (Derosa et al, 2018; Ruiz-Patiño, 2020). This likely reflects limited statistical power, heterogeneity in exposure definitions, and incomplete reporting of cumulative dose and duration.\"\n    - \"In a subset of retrospective studies, information on antibiotic classes was reported, with beta-lactams and fluoroquinolones being the most frequently prescribed agents. However, most studies did not provide detailed data on antibiotic class, duration, or indication, precluding reliable assessment of class-specific effects...\"\n    - \"These antibiotics are known to exert profound and sustained effects on gut microbial diversity, raising the possibility that spectrum of activity, rather than antibiotic class per se, may be a critical determinant...\"\n    - Conclusion on class-specific: Unresolved. Most studies report no significant difference, but this is likely due to low power/heterogeneity/incomplete reporting. Spectrum of activity might matter more than class. Narrow-spectrum/shorter courses theoretically less detrimental but untested clinically.\n    *Scan for \"pre-treatment vs concurrent exposure\" / \"timing\" / \"pATB\" / \"cATB\":*\n    - Pinato et al. (2019): Distinguished prior exposure (pATB) within 30 days before ICI initiation vs concurrent (cATB). Found only pATB associated with worse outcomes. cATB not associated with impaired survival. Highlighted importance of timing.\n    - Chorti et al. (2024): Antibiotic exposure within 60 days prior associated with worse PFS/OS. Use after start of immunotherapy not associated with impaired outcomes. Highlights importance of timing.\n    - Crespin et al. (2023) Meta-analysis: Strongest negative effects observed when antibiotics administered shortly before or after treatment initiation.\n    - Discussion section: \"Timing of exposure appears to be a critical determinant, with antibiotics administered prior to immune checkpoint inhibitor initiation consistently associated with worse outcomes, whereas concurrent or post-treatment exposure shows more variable effects.\"\n    - Strength of evidence for pre-treatment: Strong consistency across multiple retrospective cohorts, tumor types, and meta-analyses. Signal is robust but observational. Pre-treatment (especially within 30-60 days) consistently linked to inferior PFS/OS/ORR. Concurrent/post-treatment shows variable/no effect in several studies.\n    - Other studies mentioning timing: Derosa (2018) - ≤60 days before. Elkrief (2019) - ≤30 days before. Hakozaki (2019) - ≥3 days before 30 days ICI. Ruiz-Patiño (2020) - ≤30 days during/before. Hamada (2021) - ±21 days. Hu (2025) - ±30 days. Chorti (2024) - ≤60 days before/during. Gambichler (2025) - ≤6 weeks before. Pinato (2023) - ±30 days. Alshammari (2024) - concurrently. Zhang (2023) - ±1 month. Bonnefin (2025) - ±1 or ±3 months. Russi (2025) - ±30 days. Kaderbhai (2017) - ≤3 months before/during (neutral finding).\n\n3.  **Structure Examples (Studies relevant to the question):**\n    I need to pick key studies that directly address timing (pre vs concurrent) and/or mention class-specific effects.\n    - *Pinato et al. (2019)*: Directly compares pATB vs cATB. Finding: pATB (≤30d before) worsens OS/response; cATB does not. Conditions: Prospective multicenter cohort, 196 solid tumors, adjusted for class/status/steroids. Use: Direct evidence for timing consensus.\n    - *Chorti et al. (2024)*: Melanoma. Finding: pATB (≤60d before) worsens PFS/OS; post-initiation ATB has no effect. Conditions: Multicenter retrospective, 578 treatment-naïve melanoma patients. Use: Supports timing specificity in highly responsive tumor type.\n    - *Crespin et al. (2023)*: Meta-analysis. Finding: Strongest negative effects when ATB given shortly before/after initiation. Conditions: Systematic review & meta-analysis, >41,000 cancer patients. Use: Quantitative strength of evidence for peri-treatment window.\n    - *Derosa et al. (2018)*: RCC & NSCLC. Finding: ATB ≤60d before associated with ↓PFS (RCC) and ↓OS (NSCLC). Mentions adjustment for ATB class showed no significant difference between categories. Conditions: Multicenter retrospective, 121 RCC; 239 NSCLC. Use: Early evidence for pre-treatment effect; addresses class-specific (null result).\n    - *Ruiz-Patiño et al. (2020)*: NSCLC. Finding: ATB ≤30d before/during associated with ↓OS; outcomes not influenced by ATB class. Conditions: Multicenter retrospective, Hispanic NSCLC population. Use: Reinforces pre-treatment signal and lack of class-specific differentiation.\n    - *Alshammari et al. (2024)*: HCC. Finding: Concurrent ATB with anti-PD1 reduces OS. Conditions: Multicenter retrospective, Child-Pugh A advanced HCC. Use: Shows concurrent exposure can also show negative association in specific complex clinical contexts (HCC), highlighting context-dependence.\n    - *Kaderbhai et al. (2017)*: NSCLC. Finding: No significant impact on ORR/PFS. Conditions: Retrospective, 74 nivolumab-treated NSCLC. Use: Neutral finding showing heterogeneity/context-dependence.\n\n    I will select the most direct ones for the examples list, ensuring each is distinct. I'll format them carefully.\n\n    Let's draft the examples:\n    1. Pinato (2019) - Timing comparison (pATB vs cATB)\n    2. Chorti (2024) - Timing in melanoma\n    3. Crespin (2023) - Meta-analysis on timing window\n    4. Derosa (2018) - Class-specific null result + pre-treatment effect\n    5. Ruiz-Patiño (2020) - Class-specific null result + pre-treatment effect\n    6. Alshammari (2024) - Concurrent effect in HCC (contextual nuance)\n    7. Kaderbhai (2017) - Neutral finding (contextual nuance)\n\n    Wait, the prompt says: \"不同作者/论文分别成项，不要把两项研究合写\". I will keep them separate.\n    I need to make sure `use_in_review` clearly states how it serves the current task (consensus on class-specific effects & strength of evidence for pre vs concurrent).\n    I will extract findings and conditions precisely as requested.\n\n    *Drafting Example 1 (Pinato 2019):*\n    attribution: Pinato et al. (2019)\n    use_in_review: 直接回答预治疗与同期暴露对免疫治疗影响的证据强度及时间窗特异性问题。\n    finding: 区分了ICI启动前30天内的抗生素暴露（pATB）与同期使用（cATB）。发现仅pATB与显著更差的总生存期（OS）和较差的ICI治疗反应相关；cATB使用未与生存受损相关。关联在调整抗生素类别、体能状态和皮质类固醇使用后仍保持显著。\n    conditions: 前瞻性多中心队列，196例接受ICI治疗的实体瘤患者；定义pATB为ICI启动前30天内给药，cATB为治疗期间同步使用；进行了多变量和倾向评分调整分析。\n    reference_ids: [\"R10\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 2 (Chorti 2024):*\n    attribution: Chorti et al. (2024)\n    use_in_review: 提供高免疫治疗响应肿瘤类型中“治疗前暴露有害、治疗后无影响”的时间特异性证据，支持预治疗暴露信号的一致性。\n    finding: 治疗前60天内使用抗生素独立关联更差的无进展生存期（PFS）和OS；而免疫治疗开始后的抗生素使用未与结果受损相关。\n    conditions: 多中心回顾性队列，578例接受一线抗PD-1治疗的初治晚期黑色素瘤患者；比较了治疗前窗口与治疗后暴露的影响。\n    reference_ids: [\"R17\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 3 (Crespin 2023):*\n    attribution: Crespin et al. (2023)\n    use_in_review: 通过大规模荟萃分析量化评估抗生素暴露时间窗的证据强度，确认ICI启动前后短期暴露的负面效应最强。\n    finding: ICI启动前后的抗生素暴露一致关联更差的OS和PFS、降低的客观缓解率（ORR）及更高的疾病进展（PD）风险；其中在ICI启动前或后不久给药时观察到的负面效应最强。\n    conditions: 系统评价与荟萃分析，纳入>41,000例接受ICI治疗的癌症患者数据；综合了多项观察性研究的暴露定义与临床终点。\n    reference_ids: [\"R27\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 4 (Derosa 2018):*\n    attribution: Derosa et al. (2018)\n    use_in_review: 提供早期关于抗生素类别特异性效应的阴性结果，并确立ICI启动前暴露与不良预后的关联，用于说明当前缺乏类别特异性共识的原因。\n    finding: ICI启动前≤60天使用抗生素与RCC的缩短PFS及NSCLC的缩短OS独立相关；多变量调整后，关联在调整抗生素类别后未发现类别间存在统计学显著差异。\n    conditions: 多中心回顾性分析，121例RCC和239例NSCLC患者接受抗PD-(L)1治疗；暴露定义为ICI启动前≤60天；进行了多变量调整以控制混杂因素。\n    reference_ids: [\"R11\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 5 (Ruiz-Patiño 2020):*\n    attribution: Ruiz-Patiño et al. (2020)\n    use_in_review: 补充非小细胞肺癌人群中抗生素类别不改变结局的证据，强化预治疗暴露信号的一致性及类别特异性效应难以检测的现状。\n    finding: ICI启动前或同期≤30天使用抗生素与缩短的OS相关；但结局不受抗生素类别影响。\n    conditions: 多中心回顾性队列，140例拉丁裔NSCLC患者（AB-CLICaP队列）接受抗PD-(L)1治疗；比较了不同抗生素类别的预后影响。\n    reference_ids: [\"R14\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 6 (Alshammari 2024):*\n    attribution: Alshammari et al. (2024)\n    use_in_review: 展示特定复杂临床背景下同期暴露也可能产生负面关联，用于说明抗生素-免疫治疗相互作用的情境依赖性，避免将“同期无害”绝对化。\n    finding: 与抗PD-1治疗同期使用抗生素与Child-Pugh A级晚期肝细胞癌患者的OS降低相关。\n    conditions: 多中心回顾性研究，59例Child-Pugh A级或早期B级肝硬化晚期HCC患者接受Nivolumab治疗；排除了晚期肝衰竭对生存分析的干扰。\n    reference_ids: [\"R20\"]\n\n    *Drafting Example 7 (Kaderbhai 2017):*\n    attribution: Kaderbhai et al. (2017)\n    use_in_review: 提供中性结果的对照材料，说明抗生素效应并非普遍适用，受样本量、暴露时机和患者选择等方法学因素影响。\n    finding: 抗生素使用对Nivolumab治疗患者的客观缓解率（ORR）或PFS无显著影响。\n    conditions: 回顾性队列，74例接受Nivolumab治疗的NSCLC患者；暴露定义为ICI启动前或同期≤3个月。\n    reference_ids: [\"R24\"]\n\n    Check constraints: \"一项笔记属于一篇论文；不同作者/论文分别成项\". Done.\n    \"finding 充分说明研究做了什么、具体发现、方法或机制；conditions 保留与结果相连的重要条件、比较对象、测试设置及其差异。定量结果要带着它本来衡量的指标和研究对象，避免省掉条件后改变意思。\" -> Checked. Metrics (PFS, OS, ORR, PD) are kept with subjects.\n    \"use_in_review 说明它对当前任务的具体作用。按研究实际做的事判断：关联分析、预测验证、干预实验解决的不是同一个问题。回答所问关系的研究用作直接材料，回答别的问题的相关研究用作背景或比较，在用途里明确写清，不把后者称为前者的答案。\" -> Checked. All directly address timing/class consensus. Some serve as contextual nuance (concurrent/context-dependent, neutral).\n\n4.  **Draft Explanation:**\n    Need to synthesize concepts, principles, mechanisms, and author's own comprehensive explanation regarding the question. Focus on:\n    - Consensus on class-specific effects: Unresolved. Most studies report no significant difference between classes, but this is attributed to limited statistical power, heterogeneity in exposure definitions, incomplete reporting of dose/duration/indication, and confounding by disease burden. Spectrum of activity (broad vs narrow) and duration might be more critical determinants than chemical class per se. Narrow-spectrum/short-course theoretically less detrimental but clinically untested.\n    - Strength of evidence for pre-treatment vs concurrent: Pre-treatment (especially within 30-60 days before ICI initiation) shows strong, consistent evidence across multiple tumor types and meta-analyses for inferior PFS/OS/ORR. The biological plausibility lies in early microbiome disruption impairing immune priming at therapy initiation. Concurrent/post-treatment exposure shows more variable/null effects in many cohorts, suggesting timing is a critical determinant. However, in complex settings (e.g., HCC with cirrhosis/infection risk), concurrent exposure may also show negative associations, indicating context-dependence. Overall evidence is predominantly retrospective/observational, preventing definitive causal inference, but the temporal signal is robust enough to warrant judicious stewardship.\n    - Structure the explanation clearly, avoiding cross-study synthesis not in the text, keeping it specific.\n\n    *Draft Explanation (Mental Refinement in Chinese):*\n    关于抗生素类别特异性效应，目前尚未形成明确共识。多数回顾性研究和荟萃分析未设计用于检测类别特异性效应，且通常报告各类别间无统计学显著差异。作者指出，这种阴性结果主要归因于统计效能不足、暴露定义异质性大、累积剂量与疗程报告不完整，以及未能充分校正感染指征和疾病负担等混杂因素。现有证据提示，抗生素的抗菌谱广度（而非化学类别本身）可能是干扰免疫治疗的关键决定因素；广谱抗生素已知会对肠道微生物多样性产生深远且持久的影响。理论上窄谱或短疗程制剂可能具有较弱的免疫调节干扰，但该假设在临床环境中尚未得到充分验证。\n    关于治疗前与同期暴露的证据强度，现有资料高度一致地表明，ICI启动前（尤其是ICI开始前30至60天内）的抗生素暴露与更差的PFS、OS和治疗反应存在稳健的负向关联。其生物学合理性在于，早期的微生物群破坏会损害免疫系统的初始激活（immune priming），从而削弱ICI起效所需的抗肿瘤免疫应答。相比之下，同期或治疗后暴露的效应呈现更多变性或无显著关联，进一步凸显了暴露时序作为关键决定因素的地位。然而，在特定复杂临床情境（如合并肝硬化、感染高风险的肝细胞癌）中，同期暴露同样可能与生存期缩短相关，提示该效应具有情境依赖性。整体而言，支持“治疗前暴露有害”的证据强度较高，跨肿瘤类型和多项荟萃分析均重复验证了这一信号；但由于数据主要来源于回顾性观察性研究，存在指示性混杂和方法学局限，尚无法确立因果关系，需依赖前瞻性整合微生物组分层的试验进行最终确证。\n\n    Check against constraints: \"解释需要具体、清楚，讲明过程和关系，避免只有空洞的主题清单。\" -> Covers mechanism (immune priming/microbiome disruption), explains why class-specific is unresolved (power/confounding/spectrum vs class), details timing evidence strength and variability, notes context-dependence, acknowledges study design limits. Matches well.\n\n5.  **Draft Remaining Points:**\n    From the text:\n    - Whether certain antibiotic strategies/classes are more compatible with effective immunotherapy remains unclear; prospective trials needed to evaluate class, spectrum, duration, timing combined with longitudinal microbiome analysis.\n    - Indication/severity of infection often unavailable, limiting ability to disentangle microbiome-mediated effects from confounding by disease burden.\n    - Microbiome profiling not routinely incorporated into clinical studies, preventing direct correlation between antibiotic-induced changes and outcomes in humans.\n    - Publication bias cannot be excluded.\n    - Impact of antibiotic prophylaxis in hematologic malignancies (acute leukemias) and CAR-T therapy remains insufficiently characterized.\n    I will condense these into a concise list.\n\n    *Draft Remaining Points:*\n    - 抗生素类别、抗菌谱、疗程与ICI启动时间的标准化评估尚未开展，需前瞻性试验结合纵向微生物组分析以明确何种用药策略最兼容免疫治疗。\n    - 临床研究中感染指征与严重程度数据常缺失，难以剥离微生物群介导效应与疾病负担/感染本身的混杂影响。\n    - 多数临床研究未常规纳入微生物组分层检测，人类体内抗生素诱导的微生物变化与免疫治疗结局的直接相关性仍依赖临床前模型外推。\n    - 抗生素预防性使用对血液系统恶性肿瘤（如急性白血病）及CAR-T细胞疗法疗效与毒性的影响尚未充分表征。\n    - 发表偏倚可能性未被排除，中性或阴性结果研究可能被低估。\n\n6.  **Final JSON Construction & Validation:**\n    Check structure: `{\"question_material\": [{\"question_id\": \"Q01\", \"examples\": [...], \"explanation\": \"...\", \"remaining_points\": []}]}`\n    Ensure all fields match requirements.\n    Verify `reference_ids` mapping:\n    R10: Pinato 2019\n    R17: Chorti 2024\n    R27: Crespin 2023\n    R11: Derosa 2018\n    R14: Ruiz-Patiño 2020\n    R20: Alshammari 2024\n    R24: Kaderbhai 2017\n    All correct.\n    Check language: Chinese.\n    Check constraints: \"不要把两项研究合写\" -> 7 separate items.\n    \"finding 充分说明... conditions 保留... 定量结果要带着它本来衡量的指标...\" -> Checked.\n    \"use_in_review 说明它对当前任务的具體作用...\" -> Checked.\n    \"解释需要具体、清楚... 不自行拼出新的跨研究总括结论\" -> Checked.\n    \"只整理材料实际提供的信息，不靠常识补齐细节\" -> Checked.\n    Ready. Output matches exactly. \n    One minor check: The prompt says \"不同作者/论文分别成项，不要把两项研究合写，再让它们共享人群、模型或实验条件。同一篇论文的多个实验可以分别成项。\" I have separated them correctly.\n    I will generate the JSON now. \n    Structure looks solid. I will carefully format it. \n    Self-Correction/Refinement during thought: \n    I should ensure the `explanation` strictly follows the prompt: \"整理这篇文章明确阐述的概念、原理、机制和作者自己的综合解释，服务于所问问题。具体研究的结果已经放在 examples，这里不用再复述成一篇小综述，不自行拼出新的跨研究总括结论。\" My draft explanation synthesizes the author's discussion points on class-specific effects and timing evidence strength without inventing new conclusions. It's aligned.\n    I will produce the final JSON. \n    All steps verified. Output matches request. \n    Proceeds. \n    [Output Generation] -> *See response.* \n    *(Self-Correction/Verification during drafting)*: \n    Let's double check the exact wording for `use_in_review` to ensure it explicitly states how it serves the task. I'll adjust slightly to be more precise: e.